B.e0={sprinkles:0,glaze:1,penny:2,graham:3,cannoli:4,tira:5,barry:6}
B.aeP=new A.l("what","What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. Somebody rolled her flat, Detective \u2014 squeezed the custard clean out of her. We traced where she fell in powdered sugar. Not a pretty sight. Barely a pastry.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.aha=new A.l("weapon","What was the weapon?","Something long, heavy and round. A rolling pin, I'd bet a dozen on it. It's not down here. One dessert could manage it alone, if they were strong enough \u2014 but two could manage it easier.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.ea=new A.l("home","Who was in the house?","Five residents, all home, every door latched from the inside, no sign of a break-in. One of them did this \u2014 or two of them together. Could be either. Mind you, they've all got a reason, and half the mess in this house has nothing to do with it. Follow the crumbs, Detective, but check where they came from.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.KU=new A.N("chart","Fingerprint Chart","",0,"A reference card from the Donut County Police with the fingerprints of all five residents, taken this morning. With it I can dust the murder weapon and see who has handled it.",B.bp,B.b2,null,B.j,B.c,!1,"sprinkles")
B.cS=new A.l("chart","May I borrow your fingerprint chart?","Take it, Detective. We printed all five of them at breakfast, and they were not pleased about it. Find the weapon, dust it, and see whose prints come up. Just remember: a print tells you who touched a thing. It doesn't tell you when.",B.c,B.c,B.KU)
B.Rc=s([B.aeP,B.aha,B.ea,B.cS],t.q)
B.hK=new A.l("unseen","Could somebody cross this cellar at night and not see her?","Easily. No lamp is lit down here after ten, and she lay round behind the barrels, well off the line from the stairs to the boiler door. The housekeeper only found her because she came down with a candle, looking for jam.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.hM=new A.l("when","When did she die?","She was stone cold when we got here at seven this morning. Call it around eleven last night. Find something that pins it down and I'll owe you a coffee.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.hG=new A.l("found","Who found her?","The housekeeper, Penny Cotta, at half six when she came down for jam. She telephoned us from upstairs. She's been wobbling ever since. More than usual, I mean.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.hI=new A.l("advice","Any advice, Officer?","Don't trust an alibi until something else backs it up \u2014 a log, a clock, somebody with no reason to lie. And when one of them tells you a thing, go and put it to the others. That's when stories come apart.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.Ve=s(["threat"],t.s)
B.hF=new A.l("threat","There was a threatening letter in a coat pocket.","\u201cJust desserts\u201d? We know those. Every confectioner in the county got one last month, from the Sugar-Free League. Cranks. They post letters; they don't pick locks.",B.Ve,B.c,null)
B.j4=s([B.hK,B.hM,B.hG,B.hI,B.hF],t.q)
B.aP=s(["prints"],t.s)
B.ai6=new A.l("myprints",u.E,"On the handles, I should hope. I roll with that pin every day of my life, Detective. By the handles. Nobody rolls pastry holding the barrel.",B.aP,B.c,null)
B.db=new A.l("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In my kitchen from half ten to half eleven, basting my Needy Souffl\xe9 every two minutes \u2014 look away and it sulks flat. At midnight I let Barry in from the greenhouse, then went to bed. I didn't go down to the cellar until morning... oh, I'm all a-wobble just thinking of it.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.Dr=new A.l("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Strict, but fair. She paid on time and never once called me \u201cjelly\u201d. She'd been in a temper with the whole household this week, mind. Nobody was spared.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.jZ=new A.l("suspect","Who do you suspect?","I don't like to stir the pot... but Miss Tira does love her aunt's fortune a great deal more than she loved her aunt.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.UN=s(["rack"],t.s)
B.aev=new A.l("pin","One of your rolling pins is missing.","My marble pin! It hung there at supper. Somebody did come through behind me about a quarter to eleven \u2014 I didn't turn round, the souffl\xe9 was at a delicate stage. Not a word from them. Miss Tira can't pass without a \u201cdarling\u201d, Graham always gives his little cough, and Barry leaves mud wherever he treads. I heard no darling and no cough, and my floor was spotless this morning.",B.UN,B.c,null)
B.UV=s(["ricotta"],t.s)
B.ah2=new A.l("ricotta","Who in this house uses ricotta?","Uses it? Nobody eats the stuff. It's the Colonel's filling. He springs a leak when he exerts himself, poor man, and I top him up on Sundays. Mind you, he wanders all over the house.",B.UV,B.c,null)
B.Tn=s(["flakes"],t.s)
B.agj=new A.l("flakes","Who in this house is fried?","Fried? I bake, Detective, I never fry. The only fried shell under this roof is the Colonel's. Well \u2014 and yours, begging your pardon.",B.Tn,B.c,null)
B.UB=s(["pinpantry"],t.s)
B.ahF=new A.l("flour","The pin was hidden in your flour sack.","In my flour? It certainly wasn't there at ten past ten, when I measured out for the souffl\xe9. I'd have broken a scoop on it.",B.UB,B.c,null)
B.Qo=s(["cannoli/decanter"],t.s)
B.afD=new A.l("sherry","The Colonel says he drank your kitchen brandy.","Kitchen brandy? There's cooking sherry, and it lives in the cupboard right beside my oven. Nobody opened that cupboard while I was basting. I'd have had an elbow in my ribs.",B.c,B.Qo,null)
B.QQ=s(["cannoli/prints"],t.s)
B.ag0=new A.l("crimping","The Colonel says he helped you with the pastry.","The Colonel? In my kitchen? He has never so much as buttered his own toast. Nobody touches my pins but me, Detective.",B.c,B.QQ,null)
B.rw=s(["souffle"],t.s)
B.KN=new A.N("ovenlog","Oven Log","",0,"Penny's oven log card for last night, in pencil: \u201cNeedy Souffl\xe9. IN 10:30. Basted every 2 min. OUT 11:30. Risen four inches. Eggs: 6.\u201d",B.cK,B.I,null,B.j,B.c,!1,"penny")
B.e9=new A.l("log","May I see your oven log?",u.r,B.rw,B.c,B.KN)
B.UQ=s(["recipe"],t.s)
B.d2=new A.l("recipe","The Senclair Cream Puff was your recipe.","So you found it. Yes, it was mine, and no, she never paid me a cube for it. I have been cross about it for thirty years, Detective. One doesn't wait thirty years and then pick a Thursday.",B.UQ,B.c,null)
B.V2=s(["saucedrip"],t.s)
B.eg=new A.l("sauce","There is red sauce at the top of the cellar steps.","Oh, that's mine, I'm afraid. When I found her this morning I went all to pieces, and my topping runs when I'm upset. I dripped the whole way back up to the telephone.",B.V2,B.c,null)
B.rr=s(["barry/where"],t.s)
B.da=new A.l("letin","Barry says you let him in at midnight.","I did, boots and all. He was blue with cold, poor crumb \u2014 he'd plainly been out there for hours.",B.c,B.rr,null)
B.r9=s(["berrystain"],t.s)
B.d9=new A.l("jam","What is the purple stain in the pantry?","Blackberry jam. Barry dropped a whole crate of my jars on Tuesday. I scrubbed for an hour and it's there for good. It has nothing to do with last night.",B.r9,B.c,null)
B.SN=s(["crumbs"],t.s)
B.dd=new A.l("crumbs","There are cracker crumbs along the pantry shelf.","Graham's. He counts the stores every evening at six, regular as the clock, and sheds while he does it. I sweep them up each morning. I hadn't got to it today, for obvious reasons.",B.SN,B.c,null)
B.Uy=s(["pillbox"],t.s)
B.d4=new A.l("pills","She did not take her pill last night.","She hardly ever did. Said they tasted of chalk and she had too much to do to have a weak heart. I'd find them in the pot plants.",B.Uy,B.c,null)
B.UF=s(["prizes"],t.s)
B.cY=new A.l("prizes","Second place, eleven years running.","And first place to my own recipe every time, with her name on the card. Yes, it rankles. It has rankled for eleven years. I frame them so that I shan't forget to be cross.",B.UF,B.c,null)
B.Uj=s(["nestegg"],t.s)
B.di=new A.l("nestegg","There is a tin of savings under your floor.","You've had my floor up! Four hundred cubes in thirty years, Detective. That's not a motive. That's a pension, and a poor one.",B.Uj,B.c,null)
B.V4=s(["scratches"],t.s)
B.dc=new A.l("scratches","Something has clawed at the back door.","Pupcake. He wants in every time it rains, and I won't have it. He sheds sprinkles into everything. He scratched at that door half the night, the little beast.",B.V4,B.c,null)
B.TJ=s([B.ai6,B.db,B.Dr,B.jZ,B.aev,B.ah2,B.agj,B.ahF,B.afD,B.ag0,B.e9,B.d2,B.eg,B.da,B.d9,B.dd,B.d4,B.cY,B.di,B.dc],t.q)
B.afe=new A.l("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the parlor, sir, at chess with the Colonel, from half past ten until midnight.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.eb=new A.l("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Thirty years I served Madam. She was exacting, as a great house requires. I shall miss ironing her newspaper.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.hH=new A.l("suspect","Who do you suspect?","It is not a butler's place to speculate, sir. Though I will say that they always blame the butler, and I find it tiresome.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.r3=s(["cannoli/where"],t.s)
B.afG=new A.l("left","The Colonel says he never left his chair.","The Colonel's memory flatters him, sir. At a quarter to eleven he rose, announced that he wanted a nightcap, and went out. He returned at twenty past, somewhat short of breath. I did not leave the parlor.",B.c,B.r3,null)
B.rl=s(["graham/left"],t.s)
B.age=new A.l("alone","So you were alone for 35 minutes. Doing what?","Practising my concertina, sir. I do so only when I believe nobody is listening. I played without a pause until the Colonel came back and asked whose move it was.",B.c,B.rl,null)
B.cM=s(["scoresheet"],t.s)
B.ahu=new A.l("gap","There is a 35-minute gap in your scoresheet.","I record what occurs at the board, sir. Between 10:45 and 11:20, nothing occurred at the board. You might ask the Colonel why.",B.cM,B.c,null)
B.rc=s(["decanter"],t.s)
B.aga=new A.l("decanter","Did anyone touch the dining-room brandy last night?","That decanter has not been unstoppered since Christmas, sir. I mark the level in pencil, and I am rather proud of the dust it gathers.",B.rc,B.c,null)
B.ah9=new A.l("prints",u.E,"On the tip of the left handle, I imagine, sir. I hang Mrs. Cotta's pins back on their hooks each evening when the washing-up is done. One lifts them by the end. One does not grasp the barrel.",B.aP,B.c,null)
B.d0=new A.l("latch","Barry says he was outside until midnight.","I latch every door at ten o'clock sharp, sir, from the inside. After ten, nobody enters this house unless somebody already in it lets them in. The gardener was, I regret to say, outside.",B.c,B.rr,null)
B.mk=s(["cocoa"],t.s)
B.d3=new A.l("port","There is cocoa powder on the wine rack.","Miss Tira came down for a bottle of the '08 port at nine o'clock, sir. I entered it in the cellar book myself. She dusts everything she touches.",B.mk,B.c,null)
B.TV=s(["jobad"],t.s)
B.d1=new A.l("jobad","She refused you a reference.","She did, sir, and the position at Lady Finger's went to another. That was a month ago. Had I wished to do something rash about it, I should have done it then \u2014 and a good deal more tidily.",B.TV,B.c,null)
B.LQ=new A.N("cellarbook","Cellar Book","",0,"Graham's cellar book. Yesterday's entries: \u201c8:00 PM \u2014 Colonel Cannoli, one bottle of brandy (helped himself). 9:00 PM \u2014 Miss Tira, one bottle of the '08 port.\u201d Nothing is entered after nine.",B.dP,B.dy,null,B.j,B.c,!1,"graham")
B.df=new A.l("records","Do you keep a record of the household?","Naturally, sir. Every bottle that leaves the cellar is entered in my cellar book. You may borrow it. I should like it back unmarked.",B.c,B.c,B.LQ)
B.US=s(["resign"],t.s)
B.d7=new A.l("resign","You wrote a letter of resignation.","A month ago, sir, on the day she refused the reference. I tore it up the same evening. One does not walk out after thirty years. One simply irons a little harder.",B.US,B.c,null)
B.Ua=s(["locket"],t.s)
B.cZ=new A.l("locket","She kept your portrait in a locket.","Did she, sir. ...Did she indeed. I had supposed it thrown away in the first year. You will forgive me. I find I must sit down.",B.Ua,B.c,null)
B.V8=s(["slipper"],t.s)
B.dg=new A.l("slipper","Your slipper was in the kennel, with cellar dust on it.","The animal has stolen my left slipper every week since it was a pup, sir. I wear them when I do the cellar book. I have asked Madam for a taller shoe rack on four occasions.",B.V8,B.c,null)
B.U7=s(["letters"],t.s)
B.de=new A.l("letters","Who is \u201cYour devoted G.\u201d?","A youthful indiscretion, sir, of thirty years' standing. Madam declined. I stayed. One does not strike down a lady after thirty years for saying no in the first week.",B.U7,B.c,null)
B.Tm=s([B.afe,B.eb,B.hH,B.afG,B.age,B.ahu,B.aga,B.ah9,B.d0,B.d3,B.d1,B.df,B.d7,B.cZ,B.dg,B.de],t.q)
B.hL=new A.l("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the parlor, thrashing Graham at chess! Half ten to midnight, never left my chair. A soldier holds his position, what!",B.c,B.c,null)
B.hJ=new A.l("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","\xc9claire? Dear old friend! Generous to a fault. We understood one another perfectly.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.nO=new A.l("suspect","Who do you suspect?","The niece, sir. Cherchez la heiress! Failing her, that gardener is forever lurking about below stairs.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.agi=new A.l("left","Graham says you left the game for 35 minutes.","Did I? So I did. Slipped my mind entirely. Popped across to the dining room for a brandy, drank it by the window, came back. Hardly a state secret, what.",B.c,B.rl,null)
B.ai5=new A.l("gap","Nothing happened at the chessboard from 10:45 to 11:20.","A long think, sir! Chess is a game of patience. Graham sat there like a boiled owl the whole time. ...He says otherwise? Well. I may have stretched my legs.",B.cM,B.c,null)
B.TW=s(["cannoli/left"],t.s)
B.ahU=new A.l("decanter","The dining-room brandy has not been touched since Christmas.","Hasn't it? Then it was the other bottle. The kitchen brandy. Penny keeps one for her puddings. That was it. Ask her.",B.rc,B.TW,null)
B.rk=s(["ledger","notice"],t.s)
B.ag2=new A.l("debt","She wanted her 50,000 sugar cubes by today.","A gentleman's debts are his own affair, sir. \xc9claire and I had an understanding. She always said \u201ctomorrow\u201d. It was a sort of joke between us.",B.rk,B.c,null)
B.UP=s(["receipt","regiment"],t.s)
B.afS=new A.l("medals","Your medals are chocolate, and she knew.","Stage props, sir! For the Fort Fondant amateur theatricals. One doesn't wear the real ones to dinner. Gravy. \xc9claire found it all most amusing.",B.UP,B.c,null)
B.UW=s(["ricotta","flakes"],t.s)
B.agK=new A.l("trace","Part of you was left beside the body.","I shed, sir. Old war wound. I walk all over this house and I dare say there's a crumb of me in every room of it. Fetched a bottle from that cellar myself only \u2014 well, recently.",B.UW,B.c,null)
B.aeU=new A.l("prints","Your fingerprint is on the rolling pin.","On a rolling pin? Ah. Yes. I helped Penny with the pastry on Sunday. Crimping, and so forth. Ask her. She was most grateful.",B.aP,B.c,null)
B.KV=new A.N("extension","Mrs. Senclair's Note","",0,"A note the Colonel says Mrs. Senclair wrote him last week: \u201cMy dear Colonel, do not trouble yourself about the sugar. Take until Christmas. Your friend, \xc9claire Sinclair.\u201d",B.be,B.I,null,B.j,B.c,!1,"cannoli")
B.ahQ=new A.l("proof","Can you prove she gave you more time?",u.v,B.rk,B.c,B.KV)
B.Sy=s(["betting"],t.s)
B.cU=new A.l("betting","You have lost a great deal on the horses.","The Gingerbread Derby, sir. A mug's game, and I am the mug. But one doesn't murder one's creditor over a slow horse. One simply backs another.",B.Sy,B.c,null)
B.Ud=s(["medalbox"],t.s)
B.cX=new A.l("trifle","Eleven silver medals for trifle.","Put that back at once, sir. ...Oh, very well. Forty years in the Catering Corps, and nobody made a trifle like mine. Those are the only medals I ever earned, and I keep them where no one will laugh.",B.Ud,B.c,null)
B.Vh=s(["toffee"],t.s)
B.cV=new A.l("toffee","What happened to this toffee apple?","I carved it with my sabre, sir. Or tried to. The sabre won. It generally does.",B.Vh,B.c,null)
B.RY=s([B.hL,B.hJ,B.nO,B.agi,B.ai5,B.ahU,B.ag2,B.afS,B.agK,B.aeU,B.ahQ,B.cU,B.cX,B.cV],t.q)
B.fd=new A.l("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","On the telephone on the landing, darling, from ten to eleven until half past. Madame Leine was describing the new spring hats in exhaustive detail.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.ef=new A.l("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Aunt \xc9claire was a sweet old thing with a very hard glaze. Yes, I inherit. No, I didn't do it. I look dreadful in black.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.nP=new A.l("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Graham, darling. He's been sour as lemon curd for a month. Something about a reference. It's always the quiet, square ones.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.TD=s(["graham/alone"],t.s)
B.afs=new A.l("concertina","Graham says he was playing the concertina.","Is THAT what it was? Wheeze, squawk, wheeze, for a solid half hour \u2014 I had a finger in my other ear to hear Madame Leine. It never stopped once, until I heard the Colonel boom \u201cWhose move is it?\u201d",B.c,B.TD,null)
B.eS=s(["phone"],t.s)
B.ahz=new A.l("footsteps","Did anyone pass you on the landing?","Not a soul, darling. I was draped over that telephone table for forty minutes and the only thing that came up those stairs was that dreadful music.",B.eS,B.c,null)
B.VC=s(["will"],t.s)
B.ec=new A.l("will","The will leaves everything to you.","And it has for ten years, darling. If I were going to do it for the money, I'd hardly have sat through a decade of her bridge parties first.",B.VC,B.c,null)
B.Sz=s(["bills"],t.s)
B.eh=new A.l("bills","You owe Madame Leine a fortune.","Darling, I have owed Madame Leine since I was a ladyfinger. She is far too fond of me to press. Final demands are simply how she says hello.",B.Sz,B.c,null)
B.cT=new A.l("cocoa","Your cocoa is all over the wine rack.","I went down for the port at nine, darling. Graham wrote it in his little book. Auntie was alive and scolding me for it at ten.",B.mk,B.c,null)
B.SR=s(["diary"],t.s)
B.dj=new A.l("diary","Your diary says you could scream at her.","Darling, I could scream at everybody. It's a diary. If I meant to do anything about it I should hardly write it down first and leave it in the linen.",B.SR,B.c,null)
B.R0=s([B.fd,B.ef,B.nP,B.afs,B.ahz,B.ec,B.eh,B.cT,B.dj],t.q)
B.fc=new A.l("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","Out in the greenhouse 'til midnight, coverin' the strawberries against the frost. Penny let me in \u2014 door was latched. Left me boots on the mat like she always nags me to.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.cW=new A.l("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","She had a sharp tongue, but she let me sleep by the boiler when the potting shed leaks. Can't say fairer than that.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.ahJ=new A.l("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Penny's got a grudge against the old girl that's older than I am. Somethin' about a recipe. And she's the one with the rollin' pins.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.Uz=s(["pinboiler"],t.s)
B.ag3=new A.l("pin","There was a rolling pin hidden behind your boiler.","Not mine, guv! When I got in at midnight the boiler room door was hangin' open, and I always shut it to keep the warm in. Whoever stashed that did it before I was back.",B.Uz,B.c,null)
B.dh=new A.l("dark","You crossed the cellar at midnight. Did you see nothing?","Not a thing, guv, and it turns me over to think of it. There's no lamp lit down there after ten. I go along the wall by feel, stairs to boiler door, same as every wet night. She must've been lyin' round behind them barrels the whole time I slept.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.U6=s(["leak"],t.s)
B.d_=new A.l("shed","Your bed in the shed was not slept in.","Roof's leaked since the spring, guv. I told her and told her. When it rains I doss down by the boiler. Nobody's slept in that shed since Tuesday but the spiders.",B.U6,B.c,null)
B.Pf=s(["graham/latch"],t.s)
B.dk=new A.l("lockedout","Graham latches the doors at ten.","Too right he does. I hammered on the back door a good while before Penny came and let me in.",B.c,B.Pf,null)
B.SS=s(["dismissal"],t.s)
B.d5=new A.l("dismissal","She was going to dismiss you.","Aye, at month end. Told me herself on Monday. Month end, guv \u2014 that's three more weeks of wages and a warm boiler. Why'd I cut that short?",B.SS,B.c,null)
B.Va=s(["spade"],t.s)
B.d8=new A.l("spade","What is that on your spade?","Beetroot, guv. Been liftin' beets all week. Lick it if you don't believe me. ...Suit yourself.",B.Va,B.c,null)
B.d6=new A.l("jam","Did you spill something in the pantry?","Dropped a crate of Penny's jam Tuesday. She ain't forgiven me, and the floor ain't neither.",B.r9,B.c,null)
B.V3=s(["savings"],t.s)
B.ee=new A.l("savings","You are buying a nursery.","Me own plot, guv. Balance due at month end \u2014 and me last wages off the old girl was to pay it. With her gone, who's payin' me? Worst thing that could've happened.",B.V3,B.c,null)
B.Sj=s([B.fc,B.cW,B.ahJ,B.ag3,B.dh,B.d_,B.dk,B.d5,B.d8,B.d6,B.ee],t.q)
