B.YZ={cask:0}
B.a7n=new A.bZ(B.YZ,1,t.Q)
B.M1=new A.N("prints","Prints on the Cask","",0,"Three sets of prints came up under the powder. Graham Cracker's are on the tap and the bung. The other two are each a whole hand, pressed flat, one on either end hoop: Barry Tart's at one end, Colonel Cannoli's at the other.",B.bp,B.b2,null,B.j,B.c,!1,"churlock")
B.Ty=s(["graham","barry","cannoli"],t.s)
B.YQ={chart:0,cellarbook:1,ovenlog:2,extension:3,watch:4,clock:5,boots:6,souffle:7,phone:8,gramophone:9,cocoatray:10,strawbeds:11,planner:12,cask:13,porthole:14,lampcold:15,chute:16,sootsocks:17,bottles:18,tally:19,seeds:20,ricottacask:21,frostlog:22,prints:23}
B.XQ=new A.aV(B.YQ,["Splendid. Now all we want is the weapon.",u.h,u.p,u.X,u.Q,u.Q,u.o,u.N,"The operator's word that a line stayed open, Churlock. Not that anyone stood at the end of it. Who heard him talking?","Thirty-eight minutes a side. How long was that telephone call? And ask the others whose gramophone that is, and where it ought to be.","A slip of paper with the time on it, written by somebody with no reason to care. That is worth more than any amount of swearing.","Somebody told us he spent two hours last night doing precisely this job. Ask him to explain the result.","She meant to catch somebody at eleven. I wonder whether that somebody knew she was coming.","Both chocks out, old chap. Could one dessert be at both ends of a cask at once? Dust it, and ask the man who keeps the cellar.","Has anybody told you what they saw from this landing? Stand where they stood, and look where they say they looked.","Never lit. Has anybody told you they saw a light out there last night?","A way into the house that Graham does not latch at ten. And whoever used it left a little of himself on the rim.","A man who walks about in his socks is a man who does not want his boots heard. Or his boots found muddy somewhere they should not be.","Half to B., half to the Col. Two names, one secret, and a lady who was about to find it out.","She worked out for herself that it took two. I should ask the butler how wine could leave this cellar without passing him.","On top of the custard, so after she fell. Penny knows every glaze and filling in this house. Ask her whose that is.","Somebody leaned hard on that end. Penny knows every filling in this house. And if there was a hand at that end, whose was at the other?","Read it with last night's weather in mind, Churlock. All of it. And compare it with what the Colonel says he saw.",u.A],t.l)
B.RV=s(["Everybody in this house seems to have an alibi, Churlock, and two of those alibis are things rather than people: a telephone slip and a pair of boots. Ask what each of those things really proves.","Three of them can be placed by a slip of paper written by somebody else at the time. The other two can only be placed by each other. Which two say they saw or heard one another last night?","Go up to the landing and look hard at what is standing beside the telephone. Then go out to the yard and look at the strawberries.","A cask with a chock at either end, and a full hand on either hoop. One of those hands came in through the coal hatch, and the other left a record playing. Name them both."],t.s)
B.ahg=new A.l("what","What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. A full cask of amaretto came off its cradle and went over her, Detective. We traced where she lay in powdered sugar. If it weren't for the chocks I'd have called it an accident.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.ahl=new A.l("weapon","Could it have been an accident?","Not a chance. That cradle has a chock each end, and both are out. Knock out one and the cask only slews round. To send it straight off the front you want both gone at the same moment. Work that out for yourself.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.TS=s([B.ahg,B.ahl,B.ea,B.cS],t.q)
B.afa=new A.l("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Strict, and getting stricter. She'd taken to counting things lately. The spoons, the sugar, the bottles downstairs. She said somebody in this house took her for a fool.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.ahL=new A.l("suspect","Who do you suspect?","I'd not like to say. But Graham holds the cellar keys and writes the cellar book, and it's the cellar she was fretting over.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.SL=s(["cocoatray"],t.s)
B.ah0=new A.l("bell","You wrote out a slip for the cocoa.","I write a slip for everything that leaves my kitchen. The parlor bell went at two minutes to eleven, I had the pan on already, and Graham took the cup through on the stroke. He wasn't back for it by twenty past. I heard Miss Tira laughing, so I knew why.",B.SL,B.c,null)
B.ag4=new A.l("polish","Where was Graham before the bell rang?","Next door at the silver, from half past ten. You can hear every fork through that hatch, and he hums when he polishes. It never stopped until the bell.",B.c,B.h0,null)
B.ru=s(["seeds"],t.s)
B.ags=new A.l("seeds","Whose glaze has strawberry seeds in it?","Not mine. Mine's a sauce, it runs. A glaze that sets, with the seeds left in? That's a tart. There's only the one tart in this house, Detective, and he sleeps by the boiler.",B.ru,B.c,null)
B.rs=s(["ricottacask"],t.s)
B.ahM=new A.l("ricotta","Whose filling is ricotta?","The Colonel's. He leaks when he strains himself, poor man. I top him up on Sundays. If you've found a lot of it in one place, he was pushing at something.",B.rs,B.c,null)
B.SI=s(["chute","sootsocks"],t.s)
B.aeS=new A.l("backdoor","Did anybody come in by your back door before midnight?","Not a soul. It's in my kitchen, and I was stood six feet from it the whole hour. Graham shot the bolt at ten and I drew it myself at midnight for Barry. It shrieks. I'd have heard.",B.SI,B.c,null)
B.Ug=s([B.db,B.afa,B.ahL,B.ah0,B.ag4,B.ags,B.ahM,B.aeS,B.e9,B.d2,B.eg,B.da,B.d9,B.dd,B.d4,B.cY,B.di,B.dc],t.q)
B.agI=new A.l("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the dining room, sir, polishing the silver, from half past ten. At two minutes to eleven the parlor bell rang. I took Miss Tira her cocoa at eleven precisely, and was detained until twenty past upon the subject of hats.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.afC=new A.l("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Thirty years I served Madam, sir. Of late she had begun to check my cellar book against the rack. I did not take it personally. I took it as a sign that something was wrong with the rack.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.afn=new A.l("suspect","Who do you suspect?","It is not my place, sir. I will observe that the Colonel treats the cellar as his own, and that the gardener is in and out of the boiler room next to it at all hours.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.aeN=new A.l("voice",u.k,"Through the ceiling, sir, for forty minutes. The Siege of Fort Fondant, word for word as he tells it each Christmas. I remarked to Miss Tira that he did not once pause to let the other gentleman reply.",B.eS,B.c,null)
B.mo=s(["gramophone"],t.s)
B.agu=new A.l("gramophone","There is a gramophone beside the telephone.","That is the parlor gramophone, sir. It was not in the parlor when I brought in the cocoa. The records are the Colonel's own. He had his memoirs pressed at his own expense, and gives them as presents.",B.mo,B.c,null)
B.SE=s(["cask"],t.s)
B.aeM=new A.l("cask","How does a cask come off its cradle?","It does not, sir, unless it is helped. There is a chock at either end, and both must come out together. I can tap that cask. I could no more shift it alone than I could shift the house.",B.SE,B.c,null)
B.agw=new A.l("prints","Your fingerprints are on the cask.","On the tap and the bung, I should hope, sir. I draw from it every Saturday for the trifle. I have never had occasion to put my hands on the hoops.",B.aP,B.c,null)
B.ms=s(["barry/prints"],t.s)
B.aeC=new A.l("chock","Barry says he helped you chock the cask on Saturday.","Nobody assists me in the cellar, sir. I should not permit it. The gardener's hands are seldom clean and the cask has not been moved since it was laid down in the spring.",B.c,B.ms,null)
B.mi=s(["bottles","tally"],t.s)
B.ahV=new A.l("stock","Thirty-eight bottles of port are missing.","Then they did not leave by my stairs, sir. I lock the cellar door at six and I hold the key. There is, however, a doorway through to the boiler room, and the coalman's hatch above the bunker opens from the yard.",B.mi,B.c,null)
B.TY=s([B.agI,B.afC,B.afn,B.aeN,B.agu,B.aeM,B.agw,B.aeC,B.ahV,B.d0,B.d3,B.d1,B.df,B.d7,B.cZ,B.dg,B.de],t.q)
B.ahp=new A.l("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","On the telephone on the landing, sir! Ten to eleven until half past, with old Brigadier Br\xfbl\xe9e at the Officers' Club. The operator will tell you the line never dropped.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.ag9=new A.l("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","\xc9claire? A dear friend, and a generous hostess. Kept a splendid cellar. I shall miss her table.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.afU=new A.l("suspect","Who do you suspect?","The butler, sir. Keys to everything and a face like a locked drawer. Not the gardener: I can vouch for the gardener myself.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.QE=s(["cannoli/suspect"],t.s)
B.af6=new A.l("saw","How can you vouch for Barry?","Saw his lamp, sir! Bobbing about in the greenhouse the whole time I was talking. Watched it from the landing window. Poor devil, out in that weather.",B.c,B.QE,null)
B.UE=s(["porthole"],t.s)
B.me=s(["cannoli/saw"],t.s)
B.ah8=new A.l("porthole","The landing window faces the front lane.","Does it? Then I saw it reflected. In the rain, sir. A soldier develops a sense for these things in the field.",B.UE,B.me,null)
B.U4=s(["lampcold"],t.s)
B.af_=new A.l("lamp","Barry's lamp was never lit.","Not lit? Then it was his pipe. A glow, sir. I distinctly saw a glow. Does the fellow smoke? He ought to.",B.U4,B.me,null)
B.aft=new A.l("gramophone","Why is the gramophone beside the telephone?","Regimental tradition, sir! One plays the march down the line for the chaps at the club. I carried it up for that. If my memoirs were on the turntable, they were there already.",B.mo,B.c,null)
B.Rd=s(["graham/voice"],t.s)
B.ahf=new A.l("paused","They say you never once paused for a reply.","The Brigadier is a famously good listener, sir. Hasn't got a word in since the relief of Fort Fondant.",B.c,B.Rd,null)
B.agR=new A.l("prints","Your hand is on the end of the cask.","I draw myself a glass from time to time, what. Graham knows. He writes it in his little book. One steadies the thing.",B.aP,B.c,null)
B.agM=new A.l("port",u.G,"Selling it? Monstrous. I drink it, sir. I don't sell it. Ask at the Jolly Dodger whether they have ever seen me. ...Any inn. Ask at any inn.",B.mi,B.c,null)
B.ahY=new A.l("ricotta","Your filling is on the cradle.","I shed, sir. Old war wound. I dare say there is a dab of me on every stick of furniture in this house.",B.rs,B.c,null)
B.UU=s([B.ahp,B.ag9,B.afU,B.af6,B.ah8,B.af_,B.aft,B.ahf,B.agR,B.agM,B.ahY,B.cU,B.cX,B.cV,B.ed],t.q)
B.agO=new A.l("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","In the parlor, darling, with Madame Leine's spring catalogue, from half past ten. I rang for cocoa just before eleven, Graham brought it, and I held him captive until twenty past. He has no opinions about feathers whatsoever.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.afO=new A.l("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Somebody who drinks, darling. Auntie had started counting the bottles, and nobody counts bottles unless bottles are going.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.af9=new A.l("voice",u.k,"For forty minutes, darling, straight above my head. That same old siege. And do you know, he never once said \u201cwhat\u201d. He says \u201cwhat\u201d after everything. I thought the Brigadier must have died.",B.eS,B.c,null)
B.aeW=new A.l("gramophone","The gramophone is up on the landing.","So THAT is where it went. I wanted a waltz at half past ten and it had vanished out of the parlor. I assumed Graham had confiscated it again.",B.mo,B.c,null)
B.UC=s([B.agO,B.ef,B.afO,B.af9,B.aeW,B.ec,B.eh,B.cT,B.dj],t.q)
B.ahD=new A.l("where","Where were you around 11 last night?","Out in the greenhouse 'til midnight, coverin' the strawberries against the frost. I could hear the Colonel boomin' down the telephone clear across the garden the whole time. Penny let me in \u2014 door was latched. Left me boots on the mat.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.aet=new A.l("suspect","Who do you suspect?","Butler's got the keys to that cellar, guv. Nobody else. And he's been lookin' sick as a parrot ever since she started countin'.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.rx=s(["strawbeds"],t.s)
B.agV=new A.l("beds","Not one of your strawberries is covered.","Ah. Well. I did the ones inside, see. Them outside beds is past savin'. No sense wastin' a good cloth.",B.rx,B.c,null)
B.Lj=new A.N("frostlog","Barry's Frost Log","",0,"A seed packet, pencilled on the back in Barry's hand: \u201cThurs night. Hard frost. Covered all the strawbs, 10 till 12. Sky clear as a bell and a full moon, bright enough to work by. No lamp wanted.\u201d",B.cK,B.I,null,B.j,B.c,!1,"barry")
B.ahv=new A.l("log","Can you show me what you did out there last night?","Wrote it all down, guv, like I always do. Back of a seed packet. Take it. That's two hours' honest graft, that is.",B.rx,B.c,B.Lj)
B.To=s(["frostlog"],t.s)
B.ahr=new A.l("moon","The Colonel says he watched your lamp. You say you had none.","Did he? He'll have seen the moon on the glass, I expect. Bright old night, it was.",B.To,B.me,null)
B.SH=s(["chute"],t.s)
B.ahN=new A.l("chute","The coal hatch was unbolted, with your glaze on it.","Coalman uses that, guv. Bolt's on the outside so he can tip a load in. Anybody could draw it. And I lean on that wall every day of me life.",B.SH,B.c,null)
B.V9=s(["sootsocks"],t.s)
B.afv=new A.l("socks","There is custard on your socks.","I shovel in me socks, guv, saves the boots. And Penny gives me the custard skins. Must've dropped a bit.",B.V9,B.c,null)
B.afW=new A.l("seeds",u.Z,"I'm through that cellar ten times a day to get to me boiler, guv. I shed seeds like a dog sheds hair.",B.ru,B.c,null)
B.aeY=new A.l("prints","Your hand is on the end of the cask.","Helped the butler chock it Saturday, didn't I. Ask him. Heavy old thing.",B.aP,B.c,null)
B.aeR=new A.l("port",u.G,"Not me, guv. Wouldn't know port from paraffin. I'm a tea man.",B.mi,B.c,null)
